          "supports": "R2",
          "locator": "#issuecomment-5871306275"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "field-policy-upper-bound",
      "statement": "policy-upper-bound: POLICY, not T1: the product caps the run at 128 bytes; an over-cap run is rejected whole, never truncated (Not a provider fact, and the provider rule is open-ended: positives reach 128 and no fixture asserts silence on 129.)",
      "evidenceClass": "unresolved",
      "temporality": "current",
      "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
      "sources": [
        {
          "sourceId": "github-com-redact-secret-redact-secret-9077241b86",
          "supports": "supported shape: project policy, the Apify precedent; the tool-verified width is 64"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "field-observed-width",
      "statement": "observed-width: the tool-verified width is 64 (Default positives carry 64; the 60, 70 and 128 positives exercise the provider floor and the policy cap.)",
      "evidenceClass": "unresolved",
      "temporality": "current",
      "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
      "sources": [
        {
          "sourceId": "github-com-trufflesecurity-trufflehog-30de073b45",
          "supports": "exact 64"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "field-dot-in-body",
      "statement": "dot-in-body: a body containing . is not claimed: only one looser NVIDIA redaction rule admits it (The dot twin puts the dot early so no run reaches the 60 floor, so it holds under the provider rule too.)",
      "evidenceClass": "provider-documented",
      "temporality": "current",
      "observedAt": "2026-09-29",
      "sources": [
        {
